From: Wig Cheng <wigcheng@ieiworld.com>
Date: Tue, 20 May 2026 08:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] plugin: relax minor-version check to allow newer-minor plugins

NXP keeps the GStreamer core at 1.26 because the imx hardware
acceleration patches are written against the 1.26 API. Ubuntu 26.04
ships gst-plugins-{base,bad,good} at 1.28 via apt, and patch 0001 in
this directory adds the missing symbols (gst_state_get_name, etc.) so
1.28 plugins can resolve their imports against the 1.26 libgstreamer.

What was missing: gst_plugin_check_version() rejects plugin metadata
with minor > current minor (1.28 plugin on 1.26 core), so plugins are
never even loaded — they fail with

  plugin "..." has incompatible version (plugin: 1.28, gst: 1.26), not loading

and `gst-inspect-1.0 glimagesink` reports "no such element". Relax the
check to compare only the major version. The runtime alias patches
provide the actual API surface; the strict minor check was the only
thing blocking the mix.

Signed-off-by: Wig Cheng <wigcheng@ieiworld.com>
---
 gst/gstplugin.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gst/gstplugin.c b/gst/gstplugin.c
--- a/gst/gstplugin.c
+++ b/gst/gstplugin.c
@@ -486,9 +486,11 @@
 static gboolean
 gst_plugin_check_version (gint major, gint minor)
 {
-  /* return NULL if the major and minor version numbers are not compatible */
-  /* with ours. */
-  if (major != GST_VERSION_MAJOR || minor > GST_VERSION_MINOR)
+  /* Major-only check: NXP keeps the 1.26 core for hw-accel plugins but the
+   * Ubuntu 26.04 rootfs ships 1.28 plugins via apt. Patch 0001 in this
+   * directory adds the missing 1.28 ABI surface so the mix works at runtime.
+   */
+  if (major != GST_VERSION_MAJOR)
     return FALSE;

   return TRUE;
--
